      },
      "message": "fix(wire): stitch a plane's open runs and read a die face's opening as 4-axis profiles\n\nThe 4-axis wire cut refused an outline of several open runs, a face with an opening, and a wall patch, and each refusal sent the user to another. The runs of each plane now go through the 2-axis stitcher; one closed ring is the profile. A die-side face with one opening reads that opening. Runs that do not close, or close into several rings, are refused by name.\n\nFixes #3209\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
